<title>SINGAPORE: UOB Bank targets 50 pct overseas revenue.</title>
<headline>UOB Bank targets 50 pct overseas revenue.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-03-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Singapore's United Overseas Bank Ltd said on Thursday it hoped to get as much as 50 percent of its revenue from overseas in future as the company diversified out of its domestic market.</p>
<p>UOB chairman and chief executive officer Wee Cho Yaw told reporters around 32 percent of the bank's after-tax profifs in 1996 came from outside Singapore, up from 28 percent in 1995.</p>
<p>&quot;My target is hopefully 40 precent or even 50 percent income from overseas,&quot; Wee told reporters at the bank's annual financial results briefing.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65 8703199)</p>
</text>
